  "worked_solution": "To find the length of Mike's plot of land, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}-1.$\n\nFirst, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-1={x}^{2}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{1}^{2}=(x+1)(x-1)\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $x+1$ meters.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14184436/assets/3cb7db95170a088abd76aaf3f10a53ce50ff445a88d99349c76892d0ff4c8a05.png)",
